  "body": "Many vise and fixture makers publish **STEP models** of their products. CamCraft can already import one and mark it as a fixture (#339), and #744 keeps it as STEP in the fixture library. What's missing is a guide, plus a check that the common vendor files come in cleanly.\n\n**What:**\n- **A user-guide page** (the docs site, #688): import a vendor vise STEP. It covers:\n  - units and scale;\n  - orientation (rotating it to sit on the table);\n  - marking it as a fixture;\n  - placing it with the setup's mates (#561);\n  - saving it to the library;\n  - its limits: an imported STEP has a fixed jaw opening, so model it at the opening you use, or use the built-in parametric vises from the sibling issue.\n- **A check with real downloads:** try a handful of publicly downloadable vendor vise STEPs (the files only, used as test input, not shipped). Record what imports cleanly, and file any importer problem found (big assemblies, inch STEP, multiple bodies) as its own issue.\n\nEffort: low (docs) plus a check.\n\n**Done means:** the guide page exists, the vendor-file check results are posted here, and any importer bugs are filed.\n\nPart of #339.\n",
